  "scope": "BREAKFAST AND BRUNCH, the full range: hotel dining rooms and Michelin kitchens at one end, greasy spoons and caffs at the other, and the mini-chains in between. NO AWARD EXISTS for breakfast in Britain, so there is no tier-A judged ranking and the guide says so. The cheap end is carried mostly by one specialist blog and one Time Out list, because the mastheads' brunch coverage stops well above GBP 10."
